      "id": "claim_f91304df630c4b8e9be0b496c1c96994",
      "statement": "pushChangesToBranch runs git status --porcelain (early return if empty), git add ., git commit -m, and git push origin <branch>; a push failure with 'Permission', 'access_denied', or '403' in the stderr is reported as { success: true, pushFailed: true } so the caller can mark the task error without losing the local commit, while other failures return { success: false }.",
